        "date": "2026-11-07T13:03:36Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): cross drill stands off the raw stock, not only the finished part\n\nStep-1 finding (before this fix): an r10 bar in an r20 raw cylinder,\nthree stations (+X, +Y, -X). The cross drill measured its standoffs from\nthe part's facets only: start and feed-entry approach at r15, the\nquarter-turn chord's closest approach r15 - 5 mm inside uncut stock.\n- mill-turn (A/B/C rotaries stated): generated Ok, verification gate\n  empty, POSTED SILENTLY: \"G00 X15 Y0 Z10 A0 B90 C0\",\n  \"G00 X21.213 Y0 Z10\" -> \"G00 X0 Y21.213 Z0\" (P0). The verify crate's\n  rapid-in-stock law stands down in Mode::Radial, so nothing saw it.\n- lathe: blocked, but not for the rapid - \"post blocked - 1 warning(s):\n  CD1: move 1 cuts past the finish surface\" (lathe_axial routes every\n  lathe Drill, cross included, through axial_warnings; same with no\n  raw stock). With the test bench's default machine both kinds were\n  blocked only by the machine-limits clause (no A/B axis stated).\n\nFix: operation/cross_stock.rs measures the part and the setup's stock\n(GenJob::stock_facets, vertex hull: a box's circumscribed radius, a\ncylinder's own) about the spindle and stands off the larger; a stock\nwider than the part moves each mouth out along its axis to the raw\nsurface with the floor kept, and its Z top feeds the end-face detour.\nEvery rapid of the chain is then proven clear of that stock and refused\nby name otherwise (which also catches a kernel gap: mouths off their\nstation's centre line chord inside the bar - now refused). A stock not\nreaching past the part, or none, keeps the part-only chain bit for bit.\nA cross drill's stamp now digests the setup stock, so re-sizing the bar\nstales it. After: start, approach and chord all at r25 (stock r20 +\n5 mm standoff); the mill-turn program posts clear.\n\nFixes #77\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
