      "message": "fix(app): cross drill proof clears the drill's edge and a wider shank\n\nReview fixes for the raw-stock cross drill (PR #82):\n\n- An off-centre hole's mouth moves out to where the drill's edge nearest\n  the axis (transverse max(|t| - d/2, 0)) meets the raw stock, not its\n  centre line; the proof's along-the-hole branch checks the swept drill\n  slab (and a wider shank's, behind the flutes) against the raw radius.\n  r10 part, r20 raw, t 9, d 6, r_d 1: the edge stood at r19.792 (0.2 mm\n  inside the bar, posted); now r20.956.\n- The proof's rim is the tool body's, max(d, shank_d)/2; the clearance\n  and hop handed to the kernel rise to shank_d/2 + 0.1 when the shank is\n  wider than the drill (cross_stock::body_clear, kernel untouched). A\n  3 mm drill on a 6 mm shank swung at z21.6 over a z20 end face (shank\n  1.4 mm in it); now z23.1.\n- A hole plunging away from the spindle is refused by name.\n- The end-face swing check runs first: the opposite-station swing runs\n  along the new pose's own axis and was misread as an approach, refusing\n  every raw-stock opposite pair.\n- Tests: the rapid floor is STOCK_R + d/2; box stock and an off-origin\n  spindle under a moved G54 with wider raw stock; the re-size test pins\n  the stale refusal; a NaN reading refuses instead of passing.\n- RECOMMENDED.md: review-fix note, stamp churn, bit-identity scope.\n\nRefs #77\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
